WEBVTT

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:28.913
Take your brother outside as
fast as you can! Now Dean! Go!

00:00:30.755 --> 00:00:32.558
Mary! No!

00:00:35.082 --> 00:00:36.864
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.802
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:41.237
Jess excuse us.

00:00:43.798 --> 00:00:45.191
I swore I was done hunting,

00:00:45.824 --> 00:00:46.541
For good.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.484
I can't do this alone.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.665
Now you're taking off the middle of the
night to spend the week-End with them.

00:00:50.666 --> 00:00:53.166
Hey, everything's gonna be OK.

00:00:53.209 --> 00:00:54.479
I promise.

00:00:56.354 --> 00:00:57.768
You think mom would
have wanted this for us?

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.716
Dean, we were raised like warriors.

00:00:59.771 --> 00:01:02.855
You have a responsability.
To dad and his cruisade.

00:01:02.988 --> 00:01:06.400
Even if you do find the thing
that killed her, mom's gone

00:01:06.796 --> 00:01:08.966
And she isn't coming back.

00:01:09.503 --> 00:01:11.632
Don't talk about her like that.

00:01:12.778 --> 00:01:13.735
Dad's gone.

00:01:13.796 --> 00:01:15.439
I've got his journal.
He left me a message.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.754
It's coordinates he
left us. It's weird, man.

00:01:17.837 --> 00:01:18.431
Hey, Dean,

00:01:18.541 --> 00:01:19.495
What I said earlier,

00:01:19.573 --> 00:01:20.919
I'm sorry.

00:01:21.498 --> 00:01:22.922
No chick-Flick moments.

00:01:24.694 --> 00:01:25.727
Yes.

00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:36.149
No!

00:01:47.228 --> 00:01:49.762
We got work to do.

00:02:28.209 --> 00:02:29.629
Dude, you're cheating.

00:02:29.956 --> 00:02:32.126
No, you just suck.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.433
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:45.434
We're fine, keeping safe, so
don't worry. Talk to you tomorrow.

00:02:54.761 --> 00:02:57.150
Hey, where you going?
My moment of victory.

00:02:57.272 --> 00:02:58.815
Nature calls.

00:03:41.039 --> 00:03:42.022
Brad?

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:45.316
Gary, what's going on?

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:05.896
I am, um...

00:05:06.598 --> 00:05:12.030
You always said roses were
lame, so, I brought you, uh...

00:05:26.897 --> 00:05:28.316
Jess...

00:05:29.376 --> 00:05:30.658
Oh, god.

00:05:35.359 --> 00:05:37.024
I should have protected you.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:40.072
I should have told you the truth.

00:05:56.724 --> 00:05:58.103
You okay?

00:05:58.512 --> 00:05:59.836
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:06:00.723 --> 00:06:02.115
Another nightmare?

00:06:07.983 --> 00:06:09.744
Want to drive for a while?

00:06:12.246 --> 00:06:15.440
In your whole life, you
never once asked me that.

00:06:15.898 --> 00:06:18.333
Just thought you might
want to. Never mind.

00:06:19.059 --> 00:06:20.154
Look, man,

00:06:20.707 --> 00:06:23.038
You're worried about
me. I get it, and ...

00:06:23.226 --> 00:06:26.934
Thank you, but I'm perfectly okay.

00:06:30.006 --> 00:06:32.415
All right. Where are we?

00:06:32.822 --> 00:06:35.497
We are just outside of Grand Junction.

00:06:39.666 --> 00:06:43.014
You know what? Maybe we shouldn't
have left Stanford so soon.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.082
Sam, we dug around there for a
week. We came up with nothing.

00:06:47.446 --> 00:06:51.201
If you want to find the thing that
killed Jessica... Got to find dad first.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:56.255
Dad disappearing, and this thing
showing up again after 20 years?

00:06:56.494 --> 00:06:58.340
It's no coincidence.

00:06:58.778 --> 00:07:02.157
Dad will have answers. He'll
know what to do. It's weird, man.

00:07:02.517 --> 00:07:05.943
These coordinates he left
us, this Black Water Ridge...

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:08.550
What about it? There's nothing there.

00:07:09.144 --> 00:07:11.621
It's just woods.

00:07:13.357 --> 00:07:16.158
Why is he sending us to
the middle of nowhere?

00:07:23.105 --> 00:07:25.405
So Black Water Ridge is pretty remote.

00:07:25.514 --> 00:07:28.881
It's cut off by these canyons
here --Rough terrain, dense forest,

00:07:28.882 --> 00:07:31.382
Abandoned silver and gold
mines all over the place...

00:07:31.507 --> 00:07:34.797
Dude, check out the size
of this friggin' bear.

00:07:37.332 --> 00:07:40.977
And a dozen or more
grizzlies in the area.

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.767
It's no nature hike, that's for sure.

00:07:44.158 --> 00:07:47.897
You boys aren't planning to go out
near Black Water Ridge, by any chance?

00:07:48.163 --> 00:07:53.284
Oh, no, sir. We're environmental-Study majors
from U.C. Boulder-Just working on a paper.

00:07:53.378 --> 00:07:54.926
Recycle, man.

00:07:55.229 --> 00:07:56.371
Bull.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:59.954
You're friends with
that Hailey girl, right?

00:08:01.273 --> 00:08:01.899
Yes.

00:08:02.337 --> 00:08:03.901
Yes, we are.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.452
Ranger... Wilkinson.

00:08:07.285 --> 00:08:09.505
Well, I will tell you
exactly what I told her.

00:08:09.506 --> 00:08:14.906
Her brother filled out a backcountry permit saying
he wouldn't be back from Black Water until the 24th.

00:08:15.008 --> 00:08:17.558
So it's not exactly a
missing persons now, is it?

00:08:18.168 --> 00:08:21.250
Tell that girl to quit worrying.
I'm sure her brother's just fine.

00:08:21.407 --> 00:08:22.737
We will.

00:08:23.519 --> 00:08:25.569
Well, that Hailey girl's
quite a pistol, huh?

00:08:25.698 --> 00:08:27.404
That is putting it mildly.

00:08:27.565 --> 00:08:31.969
Actually, you know what would help is if I
could show her a copy of that backcountry permit.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:35.670
You know, so she could see
her brother's return date.

00:08:36.973 --> 00:08:39.445
Yeah. Heh heh.

00:08:39.586 --> 00:08:41.385
What, are you cruising
for a hookup or something?

00:08:41.447 --> 00:08:42.198
What do you mean?

00:08:42.312 --> 00:08:44.851
The coordinates point to Black Water
Ridge. So what are we waiting for?

00:08:44.852 --> 00:08:48.352
Let's just go find dad.
Why even talk to this girl?

00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:52.669
I don't know, maybe we should know what we're
walking into before we actually walk into it.

00:08:53.591 --> 00:08:54.530
What?

00:08:54.608 --> 00:08:57.910
Since when are you all "shoot
first, ask questions later" anyway?

00:08:58.176 --> 00:08:59.599
Since now.

00:09:01.524 --> 00:09:03.057
Oh, really?

00:09:06.563 --> 00:09:08.159
You must be Hailey Collins.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:12.302
I'm Dean, this is Sam. We're rangers with the
park service. Ranger Wilkinson sent us over.

00:09:12.303 --> 00:09:16.003
We wanted to ask you some
questions about your brother Tommy.

00:09:16.941 --> 00:09:18.756
Let me see some I.D.

00:09:21.659 --> 00:09:22.911
There you go.

00:09:29.701 --> 00:09:32.439
Come on in. Thanks.

00:09:33.644 --> 00:09:34.504
That yours?

00:09:34.739 --> 00:09:35.318
Yeah.

00:09:35.459 --> 00:09:36.570
Nice car.

00:09:41.491 --> 00:09:45.324
So, if Tommy's not due back for a
while, how do you know something's wrong?

00:09:45.563 --> 00:09:49.791
He checks in every day by cell. He
e-Mails photos, stupid little videos.

00:09:49.792 --> 00:09:52.292
But we haven't heard anything
in over three days now.

00:09:52.553 --> 00:09:54.493
Well, maybe he can't get cell reception.

00:09:54.795 --> 00:09:56.485
He's got a satellite phone, too.

00:09:56.876 --> 00:10:01.538
Could it be he's just having fun and
forgot to check in? He wouldn't do that.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.944
Our parents are gone. It's
just my two brothers and me.

00:10:05.945 --> 00:10:08.445
We all keep pretty
close tabs on each other.

00:10:09.023 --> 00:10:11.870
Can I see the pictures
he sent you? Yeah.

00:10:12.762 --> 00:10:14.186
That's Tommy.

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:23.544
Hey, Hailey. Day six. We're
still out near Black Water Ridge.

00:10:23.545 --> 00:10:27.545
We're fine, keeping safe, so don't
worry, okay? Talk to you tomorrow.

00:10:29.222 --> 00:10:32.464
We'll find your brother. We're heading
out to Black Water Ridge first thing.

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:34.965
Then maybe I'll see you there.

00:10:35.918 --> 00:10:36.779
Look.

00:10:36.971 --> 00:10:38.817
I can't sit around here anymore,

00:10:39.052 --> 00:10:42.916
So I hired a guide. I'm heading out in the
morning, and I'm gonna find Tommy myself.

00:10:43.672 --> 00:10:45.951
I think I know how you feel.

00:10:48.084 --> 00:10:50.400
Hey, you mind forwarding these to me?

00:10:50.666 --> 00:10:51.636
Sure.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:59.909
So, Black Water Ridge doesn't get a
lot of traffic-Local campers mostly--

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:04.910
But, still, this past april, two hikers went
missing out there. They were never found.

00:11:04.977 --> 00:11:06.291
Any before that?

00:11:06.369 --> 00:11:06.980
Yeah.

00:11:07.027 --> 00:11:10.067
In 1982, eight different people
all vanished in the same year.

00:11:10.068 --> 00:11:12.268
Authorities said it
was a grizzly attack.

00:11:12.268 --> 00:11:17.468
And, again, in 1959, and
again, before that, in 1936.

00:11:17.577 --> 00:11:20.844
Every 23 years, just like clockwork.

00:11:21.285 --> 00:11:22.804
Okay, watch this.

00:11:23.033 --> 00:11:24.650
Here's the clincher.

00:11:25.538 --> 00:11:30.438
I downloaded that guy Tommy's
video to the laptop. Check this out.

00:11:31.778 --> 00:11:33.264
Do it again.

00:11:36.358 --> 00:11:41.699
That's three frames. It's a fraction of a
second. Whatever that thing is, it can move.

00:11:42.663 --> 00:11:44.999
I told you something weird was going on.

00:11:45.326 --> 00:11:47.972
Yeah. I got one more thing.

00:11:48.098 --> 00:11:53.030
In '59, one camper survived the
supposed grizzly attack, just a kid

00:11:53.227 --> 00:11:55.317
Barely crawled out of the woods alive.

00:11:55.657 --> 00:11:57.065
Is there a name?

00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:01.684
Look, ranger, I don't know why
you're asking me about this.

00:12:01.826 --> 00:12:04.673
It's public record. I was a kid.

00:12:04.876 --> 00:12:07.223
My parents got mauled by a... grizzly?

00:12:07.418 --> 00:12:08.904
That's what attacked them?

00:12:17.215 --> 00:12:19.452
The other people that
went missing that year,

00:12:19.656 --> 00:12:21.690
Those bear attacks, too?

00:12:23.928 --> 00:12:26.432
What about all the people
that went missing this year?

00:12:27.151 --> 00:12:28.747
Same thing?

00:12:30.848 --> 00:12:34.990
If we knew what we were dealing
with, we might be able to stop it.

00:12:36.919 --> 00:12:39.547
I seriously doubt that.

00:12:39.954 --> 00:12:41.033
Anyways,

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:44.689
I don't see the
difference it would make.

00:12:45.972 --> 00:12:47.849
You wouldn't believe me.

00:12:48.178 --> 00:12:50.399
Nobody ever did.

00:12:53.135 --> 00:12:54.622
Mr. Shaw

00:12:57.688 --> 00:12:59.565
What did you see?

00:13:04.146 --> 00:13:05.585
Nothing.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.404
It moved too fast to see.

00:13:10.451 --> 00:13:12.062
It hid too well.

00:13:12.176 --> 00:13:13.663
I heard it, though.

00:13:14.257 --> 00:13:16.228
A roar

00:13:17.981 --> 00:13:18.873
Like ...

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:22.526
No man or animal I ever heard.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.619
It came at night?

00:13:25.308 --> 00:13:27.185
Got inside your tent?

00:13:27.503 --> 00:13:29.991
It got inside our cabin.

00:13:30.789 --> 00:13:34.669
I was sleeping in front of
the fireplace when it came in.

00:13:35.315 --> 00:13:38.397
It didn't smash a
window or break the door,

00:13:39.043 --> 00:13:41.062
It unlocked it.

00:13:41.844 --> 00:13:45.693
Do you know of a bear that
could do something like that?

00:13:46.355 --> 00:13:50.188
I didn't even wake up until
I heard my parents screaming.

00:13:50.423 --> 00:13:51.565
It killed them?

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:53.974
Dragged them off into the night.

00:13:56.508 --> 00:14:01.843
Why it left me alive --I've been
asking myself that ever since.

00:14:06.275 --> 00:14:08.450
It did leave me this, though.

00:14:18.407 --> 00:14:22.271
There's something evil in those woods.

00:14:25.009 --> 00:14:27.403
It was some sort of a demon.

00:14:27.877 --> 00:14:31.401
Spirits and demons don't have to unlock
doors. They just go through the walls.

00:14:31.402 --> 00:14:34.402
So it's probably something
else -Something corporeal.

00:14:34.531 --> 00:14:35.626
"Corporeal"?

00:14:35.892 --> 00:14:37.144
Excuse me, professor.

00:14:37.289 --> 00:14:39.151
Shut up. So, what do you think?

00:14:39.667 --> 00:14:42.108
The claws, the speed that it moves.

00:14:42.436 --> 00:14:44.580
It could be a skinwalker,
maybe a black dog

00:14:44.734 --> 00:14:49.365
Whatever we're talking about, we're talking
about a creature, and it's corporeal,

00:14:49.506 --> 00:14:51.623
Which means we can kill it.

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:11.023
We cannot let that
Hailey girl go out there.

00:15:11.085 --> 00:15:14.843
Oh yeah, what are we gonna tell her she can't go
into the woods because of a big, scary monster?

00:15:14.844 --> 00:15:16.844
Yeah.

00:15:17.583 --> 00:15:18.929
Her brother's missing, Sam.

00:15:19.132 --> 00:15:20.837
She's not just gonna sit this out.

00:15:21.135 --> 00:15:25.333
No, we go with her, we protect her, and we keep
our eyes peeled for our fuzzy predator friend

00:15:25.427 --> 00:15:27.351
So finding dad's not enough?

00:15:29.749 --> 00:15:31.955
Now we got to babysit, too?

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:35.726
What?

00:15:37.024 --> 00:15:38.057
Nothing.

00:15:45.091 --> 00:15:48.193
I'll tell you again. I
don't think ben should come.

00:15:48.804 --> 00:15:50.008
Roy...

00:15:50.483 --> 00:15:55.239
Look, you're paying me good money to keep
everybody safe. I think Ben's safest at home.

00:16:05.503 --> 00:16:07.145
You guys got room for two more?

00:16:07.338 --> 00:16:09.012
You want to come with us?

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:09.998
Who are these guys?

00:16:10.045 --> 00:16:13.409
Apparently, this is all the
park service could muster up.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:14.775
You're rangers?

00:16:14.822 --> 00:16:15.666
That's right.

00:16:15.823 --> 00:16:18.874
And you're hiking out
in biker boots and jeans?

00:16:20.141 --> 00:16:22.801
Well, sweet heart, I don't do shorts.

00:16:24.767 --> 00:16:29.163
Oh, you think this is funny? It's dangerous
backcountry out there. Her brother might be hurt.

00:16:31.541 --> 00:16:34.091
Believe me, I know how
dangerous it can be.

00:16:34.652 --> 00:16:37.124
We just want to help them
find their brother. That's all.

00:17:35.554 --> 00:17:37.885
Roy, you said you did a little hunting.

00:17:38.156 --> 00:17:40.143
Yeah, more than a little.

00:17:42.052 --> 00:17:43.761
What kind of furry critters do you hunt?

00:17:43.918 --> 00:17:46.405
Mostly buck. Sometimes bear.

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:51.443
Tell me, uh, Bambi or
Yogi ever hunt you back?

00:17:55.456 --> 00:17:57.678
What you doing, Roy?

00:18:03.674 --> 00:18:06.303
You should watch where
you're stepping... ranger.

00:18:10.199 --> 00:18:12.311
It's a bear trap.

00:18:18.423 --> 00:18:20.707
You didn't pack any provisions.

00:18:20.816 --> 00:18:22.646
You guys are carrying a duffel bag.

00:18:22.756 --> 00:18:25.822
You're not rangers, so
who the hell are you?

00:18:34.392 --> 00:18:36.316
Sam and I are brothers,

00:18:36.614 --> 00:18:38.241
And we're looking for our father.

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:39.876
He might be here. We don't know.

00:18:40.016 --> 00:18:42.989
I just figured that you and
me, we're in the same boat.

00:18:44.637 --> 00:18:48.282
Why didn't you just tell me that
from the start? I'm telling you now.

00:18:48.767 --> 00:18:51.850
Besides, it's probably the most
honest I've ever been with a woman...

00:18:52.397 --> 00:18:53.664
Ever.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.391
So, we okay?

00:19:00.381 --> 00:19:02.196
Yeah, okay.

00:19:02.717 --> 00:19:05.048
And what do you mean I
didn't pack provisions?

00:19:21.827 --> 00:19:23.282
This is it.

00:19:23.689 --> 00:19:24.893
Black Water Ridge.

00:19:24.956 --> 00:19:26.818
What coordinates are we at?

00:19:30.776 --> 00:19:32.987
35 and minus 111.

00:19:38.322 --> 00:19:39.323
You hear that?

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:40.543
Yeah.

00:19:42.149 --> 00:19:43.901
Not even crickets.

00:19:44.668 --> 00:19:46.561
I'm gonna go take a look around.

00:19:46.926 --> 00:19:49.194
You shouldn't go off by yourself.

00:19:49.304 --> 00:19:52.746
That's sweet. Don't worry about me.

00:20:00.836 --> 00:20:04.701
All right, everybody
stays together. Let's go.

00:20:13.379 --> 00:20:15.413
Hailey! Over here!

00:20:23.007 --> 00:20:24.337
Oh, my god.

00:20:24.728 --> 00:20:26.496
Looks like a grizzly.

00:20:43.107 --> 00:20:44.280
Tommy?

00:20:46.079 --> 00:20:47.174
Tommy!

00:20:47.644 --> 00:20:50.151
Tommy! Shh... Shh...

00:20:50.945 --> 00:20:51.899
Why?

00:20:52.337 --> 00:20:53.964
Something might still be out there.

00:20:54.845 --> 00:20:55.878
Sam.

00:21:03.439 --> 00:21:05.931
The bodies were dragged
from the campsite.

00:21:07.042 --> 00:21:10.140
But here, the tracks just vanish.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.158
It's weird.

00:21:14.317 --> 00:21:16.570
I tell you what.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:19.590
It's no skinwalker or black dog.

00:21:42.603 --> 00:21:44.981
Hey, he could still be alive.

00:21:48.876 --> 00:21:51.020
Help!

00:22:12.497 --> 00:22:15.329
It seemed like it was coming
from around here, didn't it?

00:22:21.306 --> 00:22:23.496
Everybody back to camp.

00:22:29.511 --> 00:22:31.075
Our packs!

00:22:31.717 --> 00:22:34.752
So much for my GPS
and my satellite phone.

00:22:34.866 --> 00:22:36.227
What the hell's going on?

00:22:36.321 --> 00:22:37.432
It's smart.

00:22:37.510 --> 00:22:39.950
It wants to cut us off
so we can't call for help.

00:22:40.169 --> 00:22:44.284
You mean someone --Some nut job
out there just stole all our gear.

00:22:44.367 --> 00:22:47.730
I need to speak with you... in private.

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:59.151
Okay, let me see dad's journal.

00:23:04.978 --> 00:23:05.854
All right.

00:23:06.730 --> 00:23:07.794
Check that out.

00:23:08.921 --> 00:23:10.188
Oh, come on.

00:23:10.459 --> 00:23:14.363
Windigos are in the Minnesota woods or Northern
Michigan. I've never even heard of one this far west.

00:23:14.264 --> 00:23:20.364
Think about it, Dean -The claws,
the way it can mimic a human voice.

00:23:20.724 --> 00:23:21.710
Great.

00:23:22.367 --> 00:23:24.370
Well, then this is useless.

00:23:29.063 --> 00:23:31.269
We got to get these people to safety.

00:23:33.345 --> 00:23:36.130
All right, listen up. It's time to go.

00:23:36.412 --> 00:23:39.963
Things have gotten more complicated.

00:23:40.594 --> 00:23:40.985
What?

00:23:41.079 --> 00:23:43.598
Whatever's out there,
I think I can handle it.

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:48.213
If you shoot this thing, you're just
gonna make it mad. We have to leave now.

00:23:48.244 --> 00:23:51.226
One, you're talking nonsense, two, you're
in no position to give anybody orders.

00:23:51.227 --> 00:23:52.427
Relax.

00:23:52.582 --> 00:23:55.148
We never should have let you come
out in the first place, all right?

00:23:55.227 --> 00:23:56.228
I'm trying to protect you.

00:23:56.306 --> 00:23:57.401
You protect me?

00:23:57.547 --> 00:23:59.751
I was hunting these woods when your
mommy was still kissing you good night.

00:23:59.752 --> 00:24:00.552
Yeah.

00:24:00.645 --> 00:24:03.398
It's a
damn-Near-Perfect hunter.

00:24:03.899 --> 00:24:05.620
It's smarter than you.

00:24:06.094 --> 00:24:11.492
And it's gonna hunt you down and eat you alive
unless we get your stupid sorry ass out of here.

00:24:11.523 --> 00:24:13.479
You know you're crazy, right? Yeah?

00:24:13.651 --> 00:24:16.268
You ever hunt -Chill out.

00:24:16.331 --> 00:24:20.508
Stop! Stop it. Everybody just stop.

00:24:21.295 --> 00:24:22.140
Look.

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:24.847
Tommy might still be alive.

00:24:25.347 --> 00:24:27.913
And I'm not leaving here without him.

00:24:32.379 --> 00:24:34.491
It's getting late.

00:24:35.602 --> 00:24:38.027
This thing is a good hunter in the day,

00:24:38.637 --> 00:24:41.000
But an unbelievable hunter at night.

00:24:41.474 --> 00:24:43.758
We'll never beat it
--Not in the dark.

00:24:45.807 --> 00:24:48.154
We need to settle
inand protect ourselves.

00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:50.908
How?

00:25:00.407 --> 00:25:03.630
One more time.That's...?
Anasazi symbols.

00:25:03.786 --> 00:25:07.525
It's for protection. The
windigo can't cross over them.

00:25:08.453 --> 00:25:10.940
Nobody likes a skeptic, Roy.

00:25:21.354 --> 00:25:24.483
You want to tell me what's going
on in that freaky head of yours?

00:25:26.215 --> 00:25:28.296
Dean... No, you're not fine.

00:25:28.984 --> 00:25:31.503
You're like a powder keg,
man. It's not like you.

00:25:32.176 --> 00:25:34.867
I'm supposed to be the
belligerent one, remember?

00:25:38.881 --> 00:25:40.618
Dad's not here.

00:25:43.012 --> 00:25:48.555
I mean, that much we know for sure, right? He
would have left us a message, a sign, right?

00:25:49.447 --> 00:25:51.262
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:25:52.565 --> 00:25:55.381
To tell you the truth, I don't
think dad's ever been to Lost Creek.

00:25:57.211 --> 00:26:00.497
Then let's get these people back
to town, and let's hit the road...

00:26:00.768 --> 00:26:04.507
Go find dad. I mean, why
are we still even here?

00:26:13.175 --> 00:26:14.676
This is why...

00:26:15.099 --> 00:26:16.961
This book.

00:26:17.399 --> 00:26:22.692
This is dad's single most valuable possession.
Everything he knows about every evil thing is in here.

00:26:22.786 --> 00:26:25.070
And he's passed it on to us.

00:26:25.873 --> 00:26:28.689
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:26:29.675 --> 00:26:32.538
You know, saving
people, hunting things...

00:26:32.804 --> 00:26:35.057
The family business.

00:26:37.617 --> 00:26:39.072
That makes no sense.

00:26:39.229 --> 00:26:46.410
Why-Why doesn't he just call us? Why doesn't
he tell us what he wants, tell us where he is?

00:26:47.694 --> 00:26:49.321
I don't know.

00:26:51.011 --> 00:26:52.560
But the way I see it,

00:26:53.921 --> 00:26:57.144
Dad's given us a job to
do, and I intend to do it.

00:26:57.504 --> 00:26:58.834
Dean...

00:26:59.569 --> 00:27:00.461
No.

00:27:01.603 --> 00:27:03.214
I gotta find dad.

00:27:04.028 --> 00:27:06.031
I gotta find Jessica's killer.

00:27:11.953 --> 00:27:17.210
It's the only thing I can think about. Okay.
All right. Sam, we'll find them. I promise.

00:27:18.540 --> 00:27:19.718
Listen to me.

00:27:19.890 --> 00:27:22.018
You've got to prepare yourself.

00:27:22.925 --> 00:27:25.116
I mean, this search could take a while.

00:27:25.872 --> 00:27:27.578
And all that anger,

00:27:27.781 --> 00:27:31.364
You can't keep it burning over
the long haul. It's gonna kill you.

00:27:32.370 --> 00:27:34.310
You got to have patience, man.

00:27:36.848 --> 00:27:38.459
How do you do it?

00:27:39.257 --> 00:27:41.494
How does dad do it?

00:27:42.887 --> 00:27:45.202
Well, for one, them.

00:27:45.911 --> 00:27:50.135
I mean, I figure our family's so screwed
to hell, maybe we can help some others.

00:27:50.437 --> 00:27:52.721
It makes things a
little bit more bearable.

00:27:57.831 --> 00:27:59.881
And I'll tell you what else helps...

00:28:02.212 --> 00:28:06.155
Killing as many evil sons
of bitches as I possibly can.

00:28:08.796 --> 00:28:10.392
Help me!

00:28:13.583 --> 00:28:14.897
Please...!

00:28:19.208 --> 00:28:20.538
Help!

00:28:21.883 --> 00:28:23.401
It's trying to draw us out.

00:28:23.679 --> 00:28:25.135
Just stay cool. Stay put.

00:28:25.267 --> 00:28:27.306
Inside the magic circle?

00:28:27.395 --> 00:28:29.131
Help!

00:28:30.622 --> 00:28:32.187
Help me!

00:28:34.612 --> 00:28:36.614
Okay, that's no grizzly.

00:28:42.082 --> 00:28:45.179
It's okay. We'll be
all right. I promise.

00:28:48.688 --> 00:28:50.613
It's here.

00:28:57.142 --> 00:28:58.315
I hit it!

00:28:58.362 --> 00:28:59.395
Roy, no!

00:28:59.926 --> 00:29:01.053
Roy!

00:29:01.663 --> 00:29:03.024
Don't move.

00:29:07.284 --> 00:29:10.162
It's over here. Ugh!

00:29:11.795 --> 00:29:12.827
Roy?!

00:29:39.572 --> 00:29:40.621
I don't...

00:29:41.090 --> 00:29:44.078
I mean, these types of things--
They aren't supposed to be real.

00:29:44.313 --> 00:29:46.018
I wish I could tell you different.

00:29:47.228 --> 00:29:49.277
How do we know it's not
out there watching us?

00:29:49.809 --> 00:29:50.967
We don't.

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:53.569
But we're safe for now.

00:29:54.993 --> 00:29:56.839
How do you know about this stuff?

00:29:59.405 --> 00:30:01.189
It kind of runs in the family.

00:30:06.871 --> 00:30:07.888
Hey.

00:30:08.983 --> 00:30:12.019
So, we've got half a
chance in the daylight.

00:30:12.320 --> 00:30:14.620
And I, for one...

00:30:15.105 --> 00:30:17.593
Want to kill this evil son of a bitch.

00:30:18.474 --> 00:30:20.351
Well, hell, you know I'm in.

00:30:20.763 --> 00:30:23.684
Windigo is a cree indian word.
It means, "evil that devours."

00:30:23.685 --> 00:30:25.285
They're hundreds of years old.

00:30:25.347 --> 00:30:31.625
Each one was once a man, sometimes an indian or
other times a frontiers manor a miner or hunter.

00:30:31.771 --> 00:30:34.931
How's a man turn into one of those
things? Well, it's always the same.

00:30:35.041 --> 00:30:36.449
During some harsh winter,

00:30:36.590 --> 00:30:39.985
A guy finds himself starving,
cut off from supplies or help

00:30:40.225 --> 00:30:44.793
Becomes a cannibal to survive, eating
other members of his tribe or camp.

00:30:44.871 --> 00:30:46.780
Like the donner party.

00:30:47.524 --> 00:30:51.298
Cultures all over the world believe that eating
human flesh gives a person certain abilities--

00:30:51.299 --> 00:30:54.299
Speed, strength, immortality.

00:30:54.383 --> 00:30:55.897
If you eat enough of it,

00:30:56.100 --> 00:30:58.385
Over years, you become this ...

00:30:58.588 --> 00:31:00.966
Less-Than-Human
thing.

00:31:01.129 --> 00:31:03.006
You're always hungry.

00:31:03.100 --> 00:31:06.949
So, if that's true, how
can Tommy still be alive?

00:31:09.124 --> 00:31:11.241
You're not gonna like it. Tell me.

00:31:11.569 --> 00:31:14.964
More than anything, a windigo knows
how to last long winters without food.

00:31:15.047 --> 00:31:18.082
It hibernates for years
at a time. When it's awake,

00:31:18.489 --> 00:31:21.654
It keeps its victims
alive. It stores them

00:31:21.983 --> 00:31:24.329
So it can feed whenever it wants.

00:31:25.456 --> 00:31:30.655
If your brother's alive, it's keeping
him somewhere dark, hidden, and safe

00:31:31.312 --> 00:31:33.158
And we got to track it back there.

00:31:33.299 --> 00:31:35.213
And then how do we stop it?

00:31:35.322 --> 00:31:36.402
Well,

00:31:36.668 --> 00:31:39.734
Guns are useless-So are knives.

00:31:40.756 --> 00:31:42.414
Basically...

00:31:42.821 --> 00:31:45.700
We gotta torch the sucker.

00:32:01.964 --> 00:32:02.981
Dean.

00:32:06.173 --> 00:32:07.299
What is it?

00:32:25.348 --> 00:32:26.615
You know,

00:32:26.960 --> 00:32:31.153
I was thinking that those claw
prints, so clear and distinct

00:32:32.800 --> 00:32:35.178
They were almost too easy to follow.

00:33:01.262 --> 00:33:05.000
You okay? His neck's broken.

00:33:05.736 --> 00:33:08.526
Run, run! Go, go, go, go, go!

00:33:17.696 --> 00:33:20.856
Come on. I got you. I got you.

00:33:30.740 --> 00:33:32.102
Hailey!

00:33:42.114 --> 00:33:43.428
Dean!

00:33:44.935 --> 00:33:48.517
If it keeps its victims
alive, why would it kill Roy?

00:33:48.721 --> 00:33:49.753
Honestly?

00:33:50.129 --> 00:33:53.274
I think because Roy shot
at it, he pissed it off.

00:34:00.883 --> 00:34:02.448
They went this way.

00:34:08.352 --> 00:34:10.495
It's better than bread crumbs.

00:35:52.674 --> 00:35:56.648
Hey, it's okay. It's okay. It's okay.

00:36:09.001 --> 00:36:10.159
Dean.

00:36:12.474 --> 00:36:13.945
You. Wake up.

00:36:14.810 --> 00:36:17.297
Dean. Hey. You okay?

00:36:19.863 --> 00:36:20.958
Yeah.

00:36:21.245 --> 00:36:23.529
Hailey... Hailey.

00:36:23.826 --> 00:36:25.923
Wake up. Wake up.

00:36:27.127 --> 00:36:28.270
Gotcha.

00:36:38.442 --> 00:36:41.431
You sure you're all right?
Yeah, yeah. Where is it?

00:36:41.530 --> 00:36:43.376
It's gone for now.

00:37:04.081 --> 00:37:04.957
Tommy.

00:37:08.477 --> 00:37:09.260
Tommy.

00:37:15.434 --> 00:37:17.030
Cut him down.

00:37:30.591 --> 00:37:32.375
We're gonna get you home.

00:37:33.287 --> 00:37:34.695
Check it out.

00:37:35.513 --> 00:37:38.048
Flare guns. Those will work.

00:37:52.500 --> 00:37:56.678
Looks like someone's home for
supper. We'll never out run it.

00:38:00.730 --> 00:38:03.202
You thinking what I'm
thinking? Yeah, I think so.

00:38:06.633 --> 00:38:09.251
All right, listen to me. Stay with
Sam. He's gonna get you out of here.

00:38:09.252 --> 00:38:10.952
What are you gonna do?

00:38:13.569 --> 00:38:16.244
It's chow time, you freakin' bastard!

00:38:16.573 --> 00:38:20.828
Yeah, that's right! Bring
it on, baby! I taste good!

00:38:28.799 --> 00:38:31.005
All right, come on. Hurry!

00:38:36.272 --> 00:38:37.508
Hey!

00:38:38.729 --> 00:38:40.997
Hey, you want some white meat, bitch?!

00:38:41.185 --> 00:38:42.515
I'm right here!

00:38:58.066 --> 00:38:59.680
Get him out of here. Sam, no.

00:38:59.681 --> 00:39:01.681
Go. Go!

00:39:02.071 --> 00:39:02.712
Go.

00:39:12.128 --> 00:39:13.067
Come on.

00:39:14.458 --> 00:39:15.413
Come on.

00:39:30.571 --> 00:39:31.447
Sam!

00:39:33.439 --> 00:39:36.552
Come on. Hurry, hurry, hurry! Go!

00:39:49.334 --> 00:39:50.836
Get behind me.

00:40:33.915 --> 00:40:36.199
Not bad, huh?

00:40:44.355 --> 00:40:49.643
That's when it circled the campsite. I mean,
this grizzly must have weighed 800, 900 pounds.

00:40:51.494 --> 00:40:54.779
So, really, I don't
know how to thank you.

00:40:57.960 --> 00:41:01.559
Must you cheapen the moment? Yeah!

00:41:02.588 --> 00:41:05.655
You riding with your brother? Yeah.

00:41:07.235 --> 00:41:08.299
Let's go.

00:41:20.375 --> 00:41:22.628
I hope you find your father.

00:41:25.971 --> 00:41:27.457
Thanks, Sam.

00:41:45.159 --> 00:41:47.458
Man, I hate camping.

00:41:47.771 --> 00:41:49.007
Me too.

00:41:52.172 --> 00:41:54.394
Sam, you know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:41:55.317 --> 00:41:57.382
Yeah, I know.

00:41:58.795 --> 00:42:01.017
But in the meantime

00:42:02.769 --> 00:42:04.537
I'm driving.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
